================================================================================
Graph / Inference — friendly provenance badge in the Inferred tab
================================================================================

Context:
In Graph → Inference, the Inferred tab showed each inferred triple's raw
provenance in a badge (e.g. "if_then:LoyalCustomer"). The "if_then" prefix is
internal wording; the rest of the UI calls that rule family "Simple" (and
SPARQL rules "Complex"). The badge now uses the same friendly labels.

Changes:
1. src/front/static/query/js/query-reasoning.js — new _PROVENANCE_LABELS map +
   _provenanceLabel() helper that rewrites the provenance prefix
   (if_then->Simple, sparql->Complex, graph->Graph, owlrl->T-Box) while keeping
   the ":<ruleName>" suffix; the Inferred-tab badge renders through it instead
   of the raw provenance string.
2. tests/units/front/test_reasoning_inferred_badge.py — contract test asserting
   if_then maps to Simple and the badge uses the helper.

